  "hooks": [
    "Nephi writes this thirty years after leaving Jerusalem (2 Nephi 5:28–31). It is a memoir, not a diary.",
    "Lehi's dream (ch. 8) and Nephi's vision (chs. 11–14) are one dream told twice: first as symbol, then explained.",
    "The brothers go back to Jerusalem twice — once for the plates, once for wives. A new people needs both.",
    "Nephi opens with the Lord's tender mercies (1:20) and spends the book proving it.",
    "The book ends with the family barely landed. All of 1 Nephi is the getting there."
  ]
